Provide the missing dyld ExclaveKit availability macro for ordinary macOS.

Sources: dyld-1323.3 (637911768f664e38e7e50b4fbf17e303e14fdc01) and
dyld-1378 (fd8d0c4d52320ebf64db34f3cb280310d905c5ae), include/mach-o/dyld.h.
Scope: macOS SDK 26.0 and 26.5, arm64 and x86_64.

The pinned header uses DYLD_EXCLAVEKIT_UNAVAILABLE in its declarations and
has no local definition. Preserve any definition supplied by the caller.
For an ordinary macOS C client, a standalone include of the raw header
fails at the first such declaration. The staged header compiles on both
architectures using the 26.5 installation and pinned Clang.

--- a/usr/include/mach-o/dyld.h
+++ b/usr/include/mach-o/dyld.h
@@ -39,6 +39,10 @@
  #define DYLD_DRIVERKIT_UNAVAILABLE __API_UNAVAILABLE(driverkit)
 #else
  #define DYLD_DRIVERKIT_UNAVAILABLE
+#endif
+
+#ifndef DYLD_EXCLAVEKIT_UNAVAILABLE
+#define DYLD_EXCLAVEKIT_UNAVAILABLE
 #endif
 
 
